untouched new books recently minted.  Topics and languages are equally varied,
and the feel of gathered knowledge is stifling to bear.  Stacks of the tomes
rise more then a dozen paces high in the corners, but the center of the room is
clear of obstruction, making place for a large desk, made from the corpse of
some King among trees.  At the front end of the desk lies a floating pyramid of
light from which can be heard a low hum.  The dank atmosphere throbs in time to
an unseen clock, though the sensation is easily attributable to a fear of the
unknown.    
