&07A&00n &07A&00n&14cie&00n&07t Ca&00t&14hed&00r&07al&00~
   Stepping inside you notice the air is quite stale.  It looks and smells as
if this place has been uninhabited for many centuries.  Cobwebs cover the pews
and floor to ceiling pillars, all carved quite intricately from an absolutely
huge single slab of the purest onyx you've ever seen.  Carved into the walls
are statues of demonic gargoyles and depictions of sacrificial rituals, along
with some unfamiliar foreign dialect.  A breathtaking and amazingly beautiful
stain-glass window more than compliments the very old interior design, the
multi-coloured light reflecting on a dusty spiral staircase that leads to the
catacombs.  Rows of large beeswax black candles perched on long pedestals and
old incense, crumbling from age, line the general vicinity of a long, dusty
black casket about eight feet in length, with the same foreign dialect carved
into the surface.    
~
