&07T&00h&07e Q&00u&14i&00e&07t Ca&00t&14aco&00m&07bs&00~
   The Catacombs are nearly devoid of light, despite the brilliant overcast of
the stain-glass rays that penetrate the heavens of this ancient chapel.  
Darkness seems to creep toward you from every angle, the atmosphere here exudes
a claustrophobic-like sensation, but yet a feeling of wanting to just rest,
collapse, and fall asleep forever.  Coffins of every style and size line the
floors, and fill carved out alcoves in the stone walls of this dank chamber.  
Closer inspection reveals highly intricate carvings of many ritualistic burial
rites, some written in runes, hieroglyphs, common, and even some of the same
dialect in the cathedral.  An exquisite display of craftsmanship takes its form
as a hand-made urn, resting in the exact center of the room, radiating pure
energy.  However, it is told that the catacombs hold a strong negative aura,
seeping the energy from whomever enters it.    
