#19321
&10The Passageway&00~
   Dust, thick from years of collection, rises from the ground as you walk into
the room.  You are standing in a moderately sized room carved directly out of
the stone that surrounds you.  Barely discernible footprints lead to the west
where they stop against a large swirling portal built into the stone wall
itself.  The portal appears blurry and without form until you relax your eyes.
Suddenly, within the portal, appears an image of Fairhaven, the Elven City.  
Since the footprints only go one direction, you deduce that that the portal is
one of teleportation.  To the east, the passage empties into a larger, more
luminescent room where it appears a lot more activity takes place.  To the south
rests a large obsidian door open wide.  Despite the open door, it is apparent
not many people have crossed over in quite some time.
~
