#19345
&06The Ancient Colosseum&00~
   A thin layer of dust blankets the crackling stone floor beneath your feet as
you walk over.  The cold still air sends shivers down your back as your hairs on
your neck stand straight up and the air crystalizes in front as you exhale.  
The hundreds of rows of seats surrounding you look so desolate and empty yet a
feeling of being watched by thousands cannot escape your thoughts.  The sun
barely shines over the enormous walls surrounding the arena, leaving it mostly
to be lit by conventional means, hundreds of torches lining the aisles.  
However a small, faint, ever moving azure glow circulates around the arena walls
below the seats, seemingly to give you the ever needed more light to see exactly
what you are doing here.  The only exit clearly visible is the convientiently
the same way you entered this magnificent feat of enigineering.  
~
